messages:
jordan: Heads-up — I'm seeing partial JSON blobs from the SSE stream whenever the auth token refreshes mid-connection. stream chunks arrive like `{\"id\":1,\"text\":\"hello` then next chunk finishes ` world\"}` and our parser throws. anyone run into this?
mei: ugh. are you on the browser client or node?
jordan: Node 18 fetch-based client. Using getReader() and reading text chunks. We try JSON.parse(buffer) when possible but race with token-refresh reconnects.
raul: If token refresh forces a reconnect and closes the socket, you can get truncated objects. How long are tokens? can we renew without reconnect?
jordan: short-lived (1m). We do automatic refresh via middleware that can trigger during an active stream. Currently we call reconnect on 401 which causes partial last-chunk.
mei: two quick ideas: (1) treat the stream as NDJSON (newline-delimited) if backend can reliably emit `\n` between objects, then split on `\n`. (2) use an incremental JSON parser that tolerates partial buffers.
jordan: example of our naive approach that fails when 401 comes mid-object:
```
let buf = '';
const r = res.body.getReader();
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await r.read();
  if(done) break;
  buf += decoder.decode(value, {stream: true});
  try{ const obj = JSON.parse(buf); handle(obj); buf = ''; }catch(e){ /* partial */ }
}
```
mei: that breaks if a chunk contains multiple objects or partial+complete. Also JSON.parse won't know if buffer has extra bytes after first object. Better to try NDJSON split then fallback to incremental parsing.
raul: snippet: accumulate buffer, then try to extract full JSON objects using bracket counting or a small state machine. Pseudo:
```
buf += chunk;
while(true){
  const idx = findIndexOfCompleteJson(buf); // implement brace balance or use a streaming parser
  if(idx < 0) break;
  const piece = buf.slice(0, idx);
  buf = buf.slice(idx);
  process(JSON.parse(piece));
}
```
mei: if you don't want to implement a parser, use "jsonparse" (npm) or "stream-json" which handle partial chunks. For browser, try clarinet or oboe.js.
jordan: good call. How about backpressure during token refresh? we can't pause the server but can slow reads. Is it safe to await token refresh in the read loop?
raul: yes, in getReader() based code you control reads. When you detect imminent refresh (or start refresh), you can await refreshPromise before calling the next read. That stalls consumption, letting the server buffer or drop — server might still write but you'll consume when ready. If server has limited buffer, you'll still risk truncation on forced reconnect. So ideally: avoid reconnects during refresh; re-auth in-place or request refresh window.
mei: also consider sending a small KeepAlive ping to server to signal "hold on"? not always supported. Another pattern: include resume token or offset in initial request so reconnect can resume from last-processed id. Backend must support it.
jordan: backend currently doesn't support resume. So pragmatic for now: (A) switch to incremental parser to avoid throwing on partials, (B) when 401 happens mid-stream, buffer final partial chunk and attempt immediate reconnect, replay buffer or drop it depending on id, and (C) add metrics/logging for how often partials occur.
raul: +1. Also add a client option max_inflight_bytes to limit memory growth and an onBackpressure callback so apps can drop or slow processing.
mei: I'll draft a tiny PR for the JS client that: implements stream-json integration, exposes pauseBetweenReads(h) option, and adds better logging for truncated-json events.
jordan: awesome. I'll attach a minimal repro (raw chunks) in the PR. For now I'm going to change parser to tolerant mode so we don't crash.
sre-bot: note: opened incident-ops ticket INC-2025 for repeated 401 disconnects during streaming for some customers — correlating around token expiry.
dev-bot: reminder: please add unit tests + a network fault test that simulates mid-chunk disconnects.
mei: action items: jordan open repro PR, mei prepare client patch, raul to spec resume header option for backend. I'll update the devex doc with recommended patterns.
jordan: thanks everyone. I'll ping when PR is up :thumbsup:
